abstract: >-
  AOSI-RFC-0001 specifies the AI Open Systems Interconnection (AOSI) Reference
  Model, a seven-layer conceptual stack for generative AI execution: L1 Physical
  Infrastructure, L2 Framework & Runtime, L3 Model & Weight Architecture,
  L4 Inference & Serving, L5 Retrieval & Knowledge (RAG), L6 Orchestration &
  Gateway and L7 Application. For each layer it defines scope, components, the
  data-state transformation performed (JSON Payload, Enriched Prompt, Vector
  Chunks, Batched Tensors, Hidden States, Tensor IR, Silicon Voltages),
  interfaces, observability signals and failure modes, together with a
  layer-isolation Diagnostic & Troubleshooting Matrix, per-layer security
  considerations and a roadmap for Layer 8 (Agentic Workflows), Layer 9
  (Distributed Inference / Federated Learning) and cross-layer Global
  Optimization. Version 1.2.1 is a Final Draft for RFC, released for public comment.
